invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_mont.c
catches: rsa_equiv_test
reason: the division by which a host object's rsa_vp1 computes R^2 divides
  the remainder's top two words by the modulus's top word even when the
  remainder's top word equals the modulus's, where the quotient passes
  2^64 and its low word is no estimate. No random modulus meets that step.
  bin/rsa_equiv_test's alternating-words modulus does, and its answers
  then differ from the 32-bit arm's.

--- old
    if (top < m[k - 1]) {
        estimate = (uint64_t)((((ct_u128)top << 64) | rem[k - 2]) / m[k - 1]);
--- new
    if (1) {
        estimate = (uint64_t)((((ct_u128)top << 64) | rem[k - 2]) / m[k - 1]);
